WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.920
Welcome to "Ear Biscuits,"

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.320
the podcast where two lifelong friends

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.320
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.153
I'm Link.

00:00:11.153 --> 00:00:11.986
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:11.986 --> 00:00:15.773
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:15.773 --> 00:00:19.200
Link is wearing sunglasses.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.200
Well, I'm wearing my
Hawaiian vacation glasses,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.990
which have a tint that
is somewhere between.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:28.823
Oh, come on,

00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:30.120
they're sunglasses.
Normal glasses,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.290
and sunglasses.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.160
I mean, they're sunglasses.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.440
But they're not tinted to the
point where I can't wear 'em

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.640
in this dimly lit room,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.490
and totally see everything
I need to see of you.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.750
Well, yeah, but I'm
just saying but they're,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.580
I mean, they're lightly tinted

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.130
sunglasses.
Yeah, but I'm trying

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:47.340
to make this a part of
my life moving forward,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.220
because this was my life in Hawaii,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.720
on my Maui vacation,

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.123
which I'm going to tell
you all about, Rhett.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.940
And you, dear listener.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.690
So, are you trying to
capture the vacation spirit

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:04.830
into more of, is that why
you're wearing the glasses?

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.663
or is it just like, no,

00:01:05.663 --> 00:01:08.580
I think I'm gonna become a guy
who wears sunglasses inside?

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.450
How could you tell?

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.370
Like Elton John.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.203
Yeah.

00:01:12.203 --> 00:01:13.036
Okay.

00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:14.010
I think I could.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.150
Oh, you could do anything you want to.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.887
Thank you, 'cause I really like these.

00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:18.630
But people will draw conclusions,

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.463
that's all I'm saying.

00:01:19.463 --> 00:01:20.340
I really like these glasses,

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.470
because they're big and they're, I mean,

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.940
they have progressive lenses in 'em.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.640
I can read with them,
and they're, you know?

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.593
They're indoor, outdoor sunglasses.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.567
Well, you've made 'em that.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.790
You're definitely wearing them.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.880
No, they're not too dark so
that you have to take them off

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.020
when you come inside,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.140
but I'm just acknowledging
the fact that it is a choice.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.700
Did I break your concentration?

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.950
It is a choice that, like,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.422
if me and you went to a meeting,

00:01:47.422 --> 00:01:49.977
and there was a guy that we met with,

00:01:49.977 --> 00:01:52.620
and he was wearing those glasses inside.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.453
Yeah.

00:01:53.453 --> 00:01:54.840
It would be the first
thing we talked about

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.710
after we left the meeting.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.360
We'd go, oh, he wears sunglasses inside.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.350
That's what we would do.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:03.090
But if the other parts of that personality

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.120
lined up in a certain way,
then our follow-up would be,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.513
but you know what?

00:02:07.513 --> 00:02:08.763
I think he pulls it off.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.530
I am secretly hoping, I
didn't wanna talk about it.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:13.789
If he's Roy Orbison.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.340
If he's Roy Orbison, yes.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.830
Why did Roy Orbison wear
sunglasses at all times?

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.600
Well, I think it was a...
I always thought

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.670
that he was visually impaired,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.010
and that was why he wore the sunglasses.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.330
Was he?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.580
I think he did have
some visual impairment,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.730
but I just think that
he was self-conscious

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.893
about the way he looked
without sunglasses.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.283
Are you self-conscious

00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:38.515
about the way you look without sunglasses?

00:02:40.222 --> 00:02:41.520
Is that was this is?
No.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.520
I mean, I'm conscious of what
I look like without glasses,

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.520
and I was constantly reminded of that

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.520
because I went on vacation with
the older version of myself,

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.080
AKA, my father.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.640
Does he wear contacts?

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.790
No, he has no problem.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.560
He has no.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.150
Vision issues.
Prescription.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.280
That's very unusual for a 70-year-old man.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.810
I know.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.220
Wow.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.050
And he doesn't have nearly
as much gray hair as I do,

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:13.980
I got that from my mom.
So,

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.530
you're gonna tell us
all about your vacation.

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:17.363
Yeah, I am.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.540
Before you tell us about your vacation,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.900
we do want to remind you about the fact

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.250
that we are doing Good
Mythical Evening again.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.440
If you forgot, how could you?

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.490
I don't remember all of it.

