00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.220
So, I wanna tell you
all about my vacation.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.363
We did go to Maui.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.797
You know, I had made the decision

00:04:16.797 --> 00:04:21.090
to do this trip pre-pandemic, and really,

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:24.300
I think I trace it all
the way back to your

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.590
family trip to Scotland,
where you took your parents

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:31.410
and your brother and his entire family.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.120
That really got me thinking,

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.290
I can do a vacation and bring
some of my family along too.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.270
I think that would honor them.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.470
I think they'd like it.
It's a possibility.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.170
So we put into motion this plan.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.475
Did anybody break any bones?

00:04:44.475 --> 00:04:46.383
Nobody broke any bones.
Good.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.590
Well, I mean, there was one injury.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.740
I'll tell you about it.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:58.710
We put the plan in motion
to take my dad and Nancy.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.277
And so, once we started filming

00:05:02.277 --> 00:05:06.693
"Dispatches from Myrtle Beach,"
and recording that podcast,

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.930
which if you wanna
listen to his perspective

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:14.580
on our vacation, that episode
of dispatches is already out,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.770
but there's plenty of stuff
that I didn't get to talk

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.350
with my dad about that I
wanna talk to you about,

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:22.533
and I can give you somebody inside scoop,

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.310
that I didn't get to in that episode.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.143
Oh, okay.

00:05:27.143 --> 00:05:28.020
I got two podcasts I gotta juggle.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.003
Yeah, this is gonna make
your life difficult.

00:05:29.003 --> 00:05:31.893
This is making my life difficult, but,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.080
on Dispatches, I kept saying, "Well, dad,

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.660
if you do a good job, I'm
gonna take you to Hawaii."

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.180
But really, we had wanted to go for years,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.380
it's just because of the pandemic,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.366
we weren't able to do that.

00:05:44.366 --> 00:05:45.199
Right.

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:47.520
And then also for like Christie's sister

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.600
and her husband and their kids,

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.920
we were like planning another trip

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:50.930
to go to Disney with them,

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.757
that got eradicated with the pandemic too.

00:05:53.757 --> 00:05:57.180
And we haven't put those
plans back in motion,

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.520
but we hope to at some point,

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.120
but just let me tell you, I
was telling Christie yesterday,

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:03.953
I was like, you know what?

00:06:03.953 --> 00:06:07.770
I think this Hawaii trip was
one of the best vacations

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:08.940
I've ever been on.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:10.200
Whoa, really?

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:15.200
Yeah, it was like the perfect
balance of doing stuff,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.494
and not having stuff to do.

00:06:18.494 --> 00:06:22.060
We booked a spot at a resort

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.040
on Wailea,

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.000
down there in the
Southwestern part of Maui.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.149
You ever been to Maui?

00:06:31.149 --> 00:06:31.982
I have not.

00:06:31.982 --> 00:06:33.330
I've been to the big island and to Kauai,

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.163
but not.
Right.

00:06:34.163 --> 00:06:36.600
Well, you and I went to
Kauai with our families

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.100
together many years ago,

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.300
so I was comparing it a lot to Kauai

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.103
when we were driving around Maui.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.830
We stayed at a beach resort.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.340
We stayed at this spot where
it was big enough for like,

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.010
dad and Nancy to have a room,
me and Chris to have a room,

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.530
and then the kids to sort things out.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.990
So it was like, it was a nice spot.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.990
We had space where people
could go and retreat

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.490
into their own zone.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.790
When you have a 19 year
old and a 17 year old,

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.750
you want to be able to like
give them their own space,

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.310
so I knew that was key.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.920
And then I knew that making plans,

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.820
but then making non-plans was important,

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.880
and I think all of that
really came to fruition

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.210
in terms of making this the
perfect balance of just a nice,

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.360
well needed vacation away.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.280
Are you like, are you
looking at your thigh?

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.563
What are you doing with
your hand down there?

00:07:30.563 --> 00:07:31.527
I'm just twiddling my
thumbs around this thing.

00:07:31.527 --> 00:07:33.270
Oh, I thought you were
looking at your phone,

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.890
then I saw your phone there.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:35.950
No, I'm twiddling this.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.290
Yeah, okay.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.123
All right.

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:38.956
Just making sure I'm still here.

00:07:38.956 --> 00:07:40.500
I just didn't know if you
were into what I was saying.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.333
Oh, I'm so into it.

00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:42.615
You're planning the perfect vacation.

00:07:42.615 --> 00:07:44.070
I didn't know if you're
scratching your balls.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:48.060
Just the perfect balance
of doing and not doing.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:48.957
I mean, the big question.
I've been listening

00:07:48.957 --> 00:07:50.010
the whole time.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.790
Honestly was, what is it gonna be like

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.950
to take dad and Nancy on this thing?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.389
Granddaddy and Nana

00:07:57.389 --> 00:07:58.606
are gonna be around.
But you just said

00:07:58.606 --> 00:08:00.140
it was the best vacation,
so do you think it has

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.370
to do with the fact that they were there?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.420
Yeah, that was the big question.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.797
Because people, guests
change your family dynamic,

00:08:07.797 --> 00:08:12.030
and often, they change the
family dynamic for the best.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.258
I have found that when we travel...

00:08:13.258 --> 00:08:14.091
People were on their better behavior.

00:08:14.091 --> 00:08:15.780
And when there's a friend of a,

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.340
one of the kids brings a friend.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.173
Yes.

00:08:18.173 --> 00:08:20.760
Nobody shows their asses much,
you know what I'm saying?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.850
Like, nobody just does
something stupid, embarrassing,

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.290
just as a complete dip,

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:28.410
because there's somebody
who's not family there.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.243
Yep.

00:08:29.243 --> 00:08:30.076
So you think that happened?

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:32.010
I do think that was the key to it,

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:36.600
plus the fact that dad and
Nancy are super laid back,

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.580
like they were super happy to be there.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.543
They don't add stress to the situation.

00:08:39.543 --> 00:08:41.250
They were along for the ride.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.569
Which is a lot to say for,
you know, aging parents,

00:08:45.569 --> 00:08:46.402
I would think.

00:08:46.402 --> 00:08:49.260
There was no control of anything, energy.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.540
It was like, hey, I'm gonna treat you guys

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.930
to come in on this
voyage with us, you know?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.820
And you're gonna love it.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.470
And then by the end,

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.927
the only thing dad said
about the halfway point was,

00:09:01.927 --> 00:09:04.410
"You think maybe I could play golf?"

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.030
And I was like, "Well, I
didn't know if it was too late,

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.320
dad, I didn't set anything like that up."

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.940
'Cause I don't play golf, honestly.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.680
I'm sorry if that's a little selfish.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:11.513
I should have golfed.

00:09:11.513 --> 00:09:12.346
But that did work out,

00:09:12.346 --> 00:09:13.800
and as he talked about on dispatches,

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.370
that was a highlight for him
is taking Lincoln golfing.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.940
But, yeah, I mean, we
really did have a good time,

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:25.940
and it was a test of our
relationship to have him there,

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.920
'cause you are living under
the same roof with these people

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.560
that you never lived with, you
don't know how it's gonna be.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.410
But they were cool, they were laid back.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.550
They were having a good time,

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:42.120
and so I'm happy to report that

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.710
it all worked out.
He's still your dad.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:48.330
Also, nine days was like
a generous amount of time.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.220
So, just in terms of like stipulations.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.061
Really?

00:09:51.061 --> 00:09:55.293
I was planning on 14 days, 2
weeks is what that is, Rhett.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.290
So you ready to come home at day nine?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.550
I was.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:00.690
Yeah.

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:01.883
Yeah.

00:10:01.883 --> 00:10:05.190
I mean, I would say that's pretty typical.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.140
When you're in the same place.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:07.973
Yeah.

00:10:09.854 --> 00:10:11.670
Were you eating the same
breakfast every day?

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.020
The breakfast got old.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.828
It was a good breakfast, like.

00:10:14.828 --> 00:10:17.100
Nine days of the same breakfast, yeah.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.580
I mean, I'd say obviously
these are privileged problems,

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.413
but I'm just saying.

00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:22.246
At a certain, yeah.

00:10:22.246 --> 00:10:23.079
At a certain point,

00:10:23.079 --> 00:10:25.170
I wasn't really getting
outta bed for the breakfast,

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:26.003
you know what I'm saying?

00:10:26.003 --> 00:10:26.836
Right.

00:10:26.836 --> 00:10:28.260
The cool thing about
going to Hawaii is that

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:31.440
there's three hours behind.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.870
So, when I decided to wake up,

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.460
it was like early in the morning.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.900
There's something...

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.590
I felt this like superiority of like,

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:42.780
being up so early on vacation,

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.510
like literally seeing the sunrise.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.958
Every day?

00:10:46.958 --> 00:10:48.090
What time are we talking about?

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.492
The first few days, like.

00:10:49.492 --> 00:10:50.550
Just because it was the time change.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.823
Yeah, I mean, I get up at
5:30, and it feels like 8:30.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.963
And like, I went out there
and did some paddle boarding.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:00.390
There was a beach right out there,

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:05.390
and you could go out there,
and just get some snorkel gear,

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:08.820
and go around this little
reef-ish type area,

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.550
and there were sea
turtles right there, dude.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:15.720
I've never freaking
snorkeled with a sea turtle.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.553
Did you touch 'em?

00:11:16.553 --> 00:11:17.700
'Cause that's a $10,000 fine.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.230
I did not touch 'em.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.240
I just looked at 'em, and they were,

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:25.470
some of them were like resting
on the bottom, just sleeping,

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:28.560
and some of them were just like floating.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.780
And you could just like swim around them,

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.730
and they were just like used to it.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.960
They didn't care.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.150
They were happy, as a pig in a blanket.

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:38.640
Any waves for paddle boarding?

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.230
Not right there.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.710
Driving around to other
sections of the island,

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:47.130
there was, I saw some people,
a lot of people surfing,

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.280
and some people doing some
standup paddleboard surfing,

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:53.250
but it early enough it was common enough

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.690
to do some standup paddle boarding,

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.760
but not really with surfing.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.190
That really wasn't the
opportunity right there,

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.170
in front of us.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.900
But, I gotta...

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.425
I hate the dog Maui.

00:12:06.425 --> 00:12:08.660
The beaches were beautiful...

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:15.900
But it's just not the same vibe as Kauai.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.290
Kauai was like, so Jungle-y,

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:23.580
and in like, these like
dramatic green mountains,

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:27.810
just like exploding out
of the ocean everywhere.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.870
And there's like, sheer drop-offs.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:34.800
Maui is more of like, you got this one,

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.530
there's like two islands
that are kind of connected

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:39.053
basically into one island,

00:12:39.053 --> 00:12:41.880
so you can easily imagine
how they were each made

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.320
by their own volcano.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:47.400
But there was a one inactive,

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.680
I don't even think you'd call it dormant,

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.374
it's just over.

00:12:51.374 --> 00:12:54.600
Nothing else to see here,
it's a done volcano.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.280
It's nowhere near active.
Spent.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:00.600
Haleakala that formed
the majority of Maui,

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:04.620
and so it's just looming in the center.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.779
No matter where you drive
around, you look and it's like,

00:13:07.779 --> 00:13:12.779
there's this cloud, it's like
this one mountain volcano

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.850
that just goes up into the clouds.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:18.030
But it has to be more
lush than the big island.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:18.863
Well, I haven't been there...

00:13:18.863 --> 00:13:20.700
But the big island is like just,

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.190
there's like very large swaths of it

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.380
that are just barren landscape.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:30.380
A lot of it was, of Maui
was farmed for pineapples,

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:31.733
I believe.

00:13:31.733 --> 00:13:34.860
So there was a lot of it that
was just like, deforested.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:39.860
And so now there's like
an old sugar plantation,

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:45.080
and there's like remnants of
where they farmed pineapples,

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.260
but it just kinda leaves it more of...

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.810
The focal point is the one volcano,

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:55.440
it's not like in Kauai
where you're driving through

00:13:55.440 --> 00:14:00.440
these undulating roads
around these huge mountains.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:06.020
It's just not that type of
a hiking destination place.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.770
Now, on the other side
of the island from us,

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:12.360
there's a town called Hana,
and then there's this one,

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:16.200
two lane undulating
road that you can drive.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.400
And you basically takes you...

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:18.233
The road to Hana?

00:14:18.233 --> 00:14:21.000
The road to Hana, it takes almost all day.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.150
And I was reading about that, and like,

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.170
basically marriages die on this road.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.550
Yeah, and people get car sick.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.900
And people get car sick.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:31.938
Yeah, especially the Neals,

00:14:31.938 --> 00:14:32.802
you gotta watch out.
Everybody

00:14:32.802 --> 00:14:34.800
in the Neal family gets car sick.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.720
I mean, if I go around
three curves, I'm like,

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.850
Christie, don't you be on your phone.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.860
Like, the amount of times
on any type of road trip

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:45.660
I've had to pull over, and had
Christie just open the door,

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.990
run a few feet, and
just vomit is just like,

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.300
I mean, I could sketch it.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.220
I could went in detail,
I've seen it so many times.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.388
Well, please don't.

00:14:54.388 --> 00:14:56.070
So I was like, there ain't no way

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:58.680
we're going on this road to Hana.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.326
So the, I mean...

00:15:00.326 --> 00:15:03.270
It would have a day of us doing something,

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.520
and then a day of us chilling out.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:08.400
Day one, take a look at dad.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.600
This is day one?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.130
Day one, baby.

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.740
This is within a few hours
of us getting to Maui.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.570
He's just laying out on a lounger.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.650
You realize this is your future?

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:17.700
Sleeping.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.110
This is my future.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:20.970
Actually, in many ways,
this is your present.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.920
He makes the same exact face that you make

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:24.000
when you fall asleep.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.050
Yeah, his mouth is open.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:26.497
And I assume.
Like the picture you take

00:15:26.497 --> 00:15:28.050
of me every time I falls
sleep in on a plane.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:30.450
He falls asleep as
quickly as you, I assume.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.740
You see that necklace he is wearing?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.450
That's what they give
you when you show up.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.448
Like, that's literally
how quick he just...

00:15:36.448 --> 00:15:38.820
Drank a drink.
He went in vacation mode,

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:39.990
so fast, I love it.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.730
And, the one thing that-

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.160
Had he been to Hawaii, ever?

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.333
He had been to Hawaii-uh before, yeah.

00:15:46.333 --> 00:15:49.229
I was gonna ask, does he
still call it Hawaii-uh?

00:15:49.229 --> 00:15:54.180
It's the same place, but
yeah, that's where he's been.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.550
So many years ago, they
went before, but like,

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.400
dude's got a lot more hair
on his body than me too.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:00.378
Has he always?

00:16:00.378 --> 00:16:01.211
Always.

00:16:01.211 --> 00:16:02.044
So you don't have that to look forward to.

00:16:02.044 --> 00:16:04.560
He's had a lot more hair than this, too.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.000
It's kind of died down.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.682
It's petered out a little bit.

00:16:07.682 --> 00:16:08.992
Oh, that's something to...

00:16:08.992 --> 00:16:11.010
See, here's me wearing
my sunglasses, I'm awake.

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:11.843
I can see that.

00:16:11.843 --> 00:16:13.050
But my mouth is open.

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.060
So, there's a number of things that we did

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:18.090
that I'll tell you about,
but first, I mean...

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:19.110
Let's talk more about-

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.340
Good Mythical Evening?
Good Mythical Evening,

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.180
did we tell you about it?

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.350
We already told you about it,

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.750
we just wanna tell you some more about it.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.940
What else can we tell you about it?

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:30.093
I know that we started to
plan some of the segments.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:33.810
We've planned most of
them, and I think that-

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:34.860
They're different.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.440
Maybe a notch up from last year.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:40.530
It's totally different than last year,

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:43.170
but then kind of, it's totally the same,

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.330
but then totally fresh.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.290
No repeats.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.000
No repeats.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.060
We're trying different things this year.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.470
Things are gonna get outta hand.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.840
Things are gonna get memorable.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.690
It was a once in a lifetime experience

