00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:45.570
So, one day we decided to go
to the top of the volcano,

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:50.520
because I found out that you
can drive all the way up there.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.700
From where we were, it's like
an hour and a half drive.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.460
And yeah, there's a couple
of places where it gets kinda

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.800
a lot of some switchbacks, and I was like,

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.570
listen, we're not doing the road to Hana,

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:03.840
but we gotta go to the
top of the Haleakala.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:04.833
Haleakala.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.120
It takes me a couple of times to get it.

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:12.467
So, we're driving up there and I'm like-

00:18:12.467 --> 00:18:14.670
How do you prepare the family for this?

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:15.540
They're gonna get car sick.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.680
We can park.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:17.940
Well, I'm just like...

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:19.260
Do they all take ginger?

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.080
Yeah, we got the ginger chews,

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.540
and we've got some Dramamine.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.970
Do they all get in the front seat?

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:27.990
'Cause you know, Christie's gotta stay

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.850
in the front seat.
Christie's the front seat.

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:30.683
She's the queen.

00:18:30.683 --> 00:18:32.400
But what are the, 'cause I mean,

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.780
all the kids get car sick too.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.937
We rented a minivan, and then...

00:18:35.937 --> 00:18:37.440
You put 'em on top?

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.750
'Cause if you get the wind in the face,

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.070
a lot of times, that'll help.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.260
I mean, it's mainly just giving
them a little bit of that

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:48.180
anti nauseous stuff, and
making sure that they're not

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.013
on their phones

00:18:49.013 --> 00:18:50.130
when it gets curve.
So, it worked.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.153
It did work.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.810
And the other thing I was
concerned about is like,

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.220
is it a long hike?

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.960
But no, you drive up to the top,

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.250
and then there's a couple places

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.140
where you can just look out.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.570
Now, the thing that people rave about,

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.580
and you have to get
reservations to do this,

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.870
is to go up at like...

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.703
Sunset.

00:19:07.703 --> 00:19:08.536
Four o'clock,

00:19:08.536 --> 00:19:09.369
it was sunrise.

00:19:09.369 --> 00:19:10.500
Sunrise.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.527
You know, you're at like 10,000 feet,

00:19:13.527 --> 00:19:15.510
and it's, you're in the
middle of this island,

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:18.480
and you can watch the sunrise,

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:23.130
and you can see all these
other Hawaiian islands.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.170
Not every single one of them, but,

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.130
I mean, we didn't.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.750
I was like, we're not
getting up that early.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.583
Yeah.

00:19:28.583 --> 00:19:29.416
So we didn't do that.

00:19:29.416 --> 00:19:31.670
You can also watch
sunset when I was like...

00:19:32.885 --> 00:19:35.643
If we get up there, that'll be a victory.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.250
So we drive up there.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:41.550
I mean, and we're like,
man, there's so many clouds.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.690
What's?

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:44.010
We're not gonna see anything.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.370
But it was so high that
we went above the clouds.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:48.570
Oh, wow.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:51.270
And it was pretty amazing,
even at the middle of the day.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.950
You got pictures of
that, above the clouds?

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.900
So we're driving up there,

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:59.150
and you don't have to hike
too much in order to...

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.550
You get out of the car,
and you're kind of just

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:06.153
at an overlook, you know?

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:11.100
And there's an observatory up
there, and stuff you can see.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.456
And I was like, well, because,

00:20:12.456 --> 00:20:15.180
I don't wanna make dad and Nana

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.640
have to do a bunch of walking and hiking.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:19.290
So like we get out and
we're like, all right,

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:23.910
you guys can go in the
information center slash museum,

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.080
and then I'm gonna take this trail

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.690
and just hike up a little bit
further to this top point.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:31.955
So, me and Lily, it was cold up there too.

00:20:31.955 --> 00:20:33.723
Like, I had to put on a coat.

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:36.630
You know, I'm cold natured.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.670
And then we walk all the way up there,

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.870
and then as we're coming back down,

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.060
here comes Granddaddy and
Nana walking up there,

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:44.400
and they say, "Well, if we're
gonna come all this way,

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.700
we're gonna do this."

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:48.450
I was like, good Lord, don't fall.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:50.970
I don't want to have a
Rhett's mama breaking her

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.410
ankle situation.
Yeah, right, yeah.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:54.750
You don't get that free
Scottish healthcare

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:55.589
when you're in Hawaii.

00:20:55.589 --> 00:20:58.620
Oh, you didn't have to
pay for any of that?

00:20:58.620 --> 00:20:59.453
No.

00:20:59.453 --> 00:21:00.390
I remember that.

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.710
Yeah, you don't get that in Hawaii.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.150
We did have to like,

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.100
get more stuff done when
she got back to the U.S.,

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.690
but I mean, the Scottish part was free.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:09.120
How's her ankle now, just as a side note?

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.150
Is there any residual
like, long-term effect?

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:15.720
Like when a thundercloud
comes up, her ankle hurts?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:20.130
There is like residual pain at times.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.410
Not debilitating by any
means, but definitely,

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:24.540
it was a setback.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.549
Just one of those things,
it's just like, oh, you know?

00:21:26.549 --> 00:21:29.103
My ankle hurts a little
bit today kind of thing.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:32.620
So I don't recommend you
breaking your mom's ankle

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:36.480
on a vacation, or your
dad's, or your stepmom.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.298
Everything about my dad, you know,

00:21:39.298 --> 00:21:42.750
I was watching him
closely to see my future.

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:43.583
Yeah.

00:21:43.583 --> 00:21:44.416
You know?

00:21:44.416 --> 00:21:46.200
'Cause it's like, I'm proud of the fact

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.790
that he could do that little hike,

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:50.370
and that he could enjoy
himself on vacation,

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.620
and that he could take a nap
with his mouth gaped open.

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.510
It's like, these are things
that I can look forward to.

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.608
Yeah, you can do that.

00:21:55.608 --> 00:21:56.441
You know?

00:21:56.441 --> 00:22:00.630
And then the next morning after
we get back from Haleakala,

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.590
we're like sitting at the
breakfast buffet, and I like,

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.960
I like caught Lily's eye.

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:09.817
And then I asked, I was like,

00:22:09.817 --> 00:22:11.400
"Granddad and Nana,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:15.477
have you just ever been
to the top of a volcano?"

00:22:16.526 --> 00:22:20.453
And they were like, "No,
I sure would like to go."

00:22:20.453 --> 00:22:24.536
And I was like, "That's
where we went yesterday."

00:22:27.087 --> 00:22:28.334
I was like, "What?"

00:22:28.334 --> 00:22:32.550
I was like, I didn't ask
any follow-up questions.

00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:33.383
I just thought it was hilarious.

00:22:33.383 --> 00:22:34.673
You didn't say anything else?

00:22:34.673 --> 00:22:36.870
I said, "That's where we went yesterday."

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:38.310
And they were like, "Oh, oh yeah.

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:39.447
Okay, you're right."

00:22:41.112 --> 00:22:43.201
It was just like, what?

00:22:43.201 --> 00:22:44.281
Do you not remember?

00:22:44.281 --> 00:22:45.831
Did they think it was a ride?

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:48.300
Maybe the way I asked it.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:51.120
Like Soarin' Over California in Disney?

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:51.953
I mean, they probably went

00:22:51.953 --> 00:22:53.130
to the orange field.
I think when I asked,

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:53.970
would you like to go to
the top of a volcano?

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:54.840
They pictured

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:57.000
an erupting volcano.
Of course,

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:58.060
Joe versus the volcano.

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.810
So it was like, it didn't
really connect to like,

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:03.210
totally dormant volcano.

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:04.860
But I'm like, yeah, that's...

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:06.003
Are you with me?

00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:08.880
Are you here for this?

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:09.713
Do you...

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:11.960
They had a good time.

00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:14.700
Whether they remembered it
or not is another question.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:17.280
I've been to a non dormant volcano.

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:18.113
I remember.

00:23:18.113 --> 00:23:20.820
I remember you guys
got in a huge argument,

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:22.530
'cause you were hiking to it.

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:24.990
Any sort of hiking, yeah.

00:23:24.990 --> 00:23:26.150
I mean, boy, it'll...

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:29.361
Jesse and I will find a way.
That's why

00:23:29.361 --> 00:23:30.420
I didn't do any hiking,

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:33.513
even though I really wanted to, no hiking.

00:23:35.070 --> 00:23:37.020
Yeah, I mean you had to do,

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.520
you gotta plan better than we did.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:40.320
It was a little too last minute, but yeah.

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:42.783
I mean non dormant
volcanoes are even more fun.

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:45.690
I know, I would really love to do that,

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:49.680
which is like a big highlight
of going to the big island.

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:50.700
Yeah, if it's flowing,

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:52.320
I don't know if it's flowing right now.

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:53.820
It was flowing when you went though.

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:55.170
Oh, yeah.

00:23:55.170 --> 00:23:56.890
Not like crazy, not like

00:23:57.900 --> 00:24:00.840
a river of lava going into the ocean,

00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:01.860
but just like, oh, there it is,

00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:03.093
bubbling along hot.

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:06.000
Hot.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.100
Eventually get into the
ocean, and it's steaming up.

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.110
I don't wanna say that
Maui wasn't beautiful,

00:24:10.110 --> 00:24:12.930
it's just the beaches
were really the highlight.

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:17.930
And as it turns out, scuba
diving is a big thing on Maui.

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:23.670
There's lots of destinations where you can

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:24.503
really enjoy scuba diving.
Well, and that's why,

00:24:24.503 --> 00:24:25.710
and that's what you've been preparing

00:24:25.710 --> 00:24:27.540
yourself for.
Yeah, that's not...

00:24:27.540 --> 00:24:29.460
I actually didn't know that.

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:31.140
It kind worked out, but like, yeah.

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:32.595
I was like, we're gonna go to Hawaii,

00:24:32.595 --> 00:24:35.790
and then I was like, yeah,
let's really get going,

00:24:35.790 --> 00:24:37.380
get into gear on this.

00:24:37.380 --> 00:24:39.120
Like, getting certified for scuba,

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:40.770
looking forward to the trip,

00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.720
but as it turns out
like that is a highlight

00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:46.080
of being on Maui even more so than Kauai.

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:47.232
Like Kauai, there is

00:24:47.232 --> 00:24:51.780
you can scuba dive probably
in any Hawaiian island,

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:53.760
but like Maui is actually,

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:56.308
according to the people we went with,

00:24:56.308 --> 00:24:59.520
'cause we went on two different days.

00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:00.353
Maui's the best.

00:25:00.353 --> 00:25:01.500
And of course, this is just me and Lincoln

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.720
because we got certified
leading up to the trip,

00:25:03.720 --> 00:25:06.600
and this is a big part of
what I was looking forward to.

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:08.067
And, you know.

00:25:08.067 --> 00:25:13.067
And you were living basically
the "White Lotus" life,

00:25:13.348 --> 00:25:14.181
you know?

00:25:14.181 --> 00:25:16.470
You were the dad in "White Lotus".

00:25:16.470 --> 00:25:19.526
Which, great show,

00:25:19.526 --> 00:25:22.590
and it really started to hit
close to home when, yeah.

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:24.330
It's one thing to like, yeah.

00:25:24.330 --> 00:25:25.620
And weren't you like,

00:25:25.620 --> 00:25:27.750
relatively close to the
resort where they actually...

00:25:27.750 --> 00:25:29.370
They filmed that at Four Seasons in Maui.

00:25:29.370 --> 00:25:32.130
Yeah, we were at the Andaz Resort,

00:25:32.130 --> 00:25:33.930
which is like next door to it.

00:25:33.930 --> 00:25:35.790
So you were next door to the set?

00:25:35.790 --> 00:25:36.623
Yes.

00:25:36.623 --> 00:25:39.270
Doing the same thing
with your teenage son?

00:25:39.270 --> 00:25:40.440
Yeah.

00:25:40.440 --> 00:25:43.440
And they had that Outrigger
canoe that you could reserve

00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:44.823
and go out on that too.

00:25:45.930 --> 00:25:48.200
When we did a trip a day trip one day...

00:25:50.008 --> 00:25:52.950
I think, yeah, that was
when some other members

00:25:52.950 --> 00:25:54.587
of the family did the Outrigger trip.

00:25:54.587 --> 00:25:56.100
Did you have an existential crisis?

00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:57.210
No, I did not.

00:25:57.210 --> 00:26:00.420
Well, the existential
crisis was during the luau.

00:26:00.420 --> 00:26:03.600
I mean, they had booked one
night we go to the luau,

00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:05.010
so I'll get back to the scuba diving.

00:26:05.010 --> 00:26:09.780
But the "White Lotus" of it
all to me was really that

00:26:09.780 --> 00:26:14.780
being at the luau, and kind
of feeling this like, okay,

00:26:15.090 --> 00:26:19.710
I'm paying this high ticket
price as a tourist to come here

00:26:19.710 --> 00:26:23.130
and eat your pork, and like,

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:26.224
entertain me with your history, you know?

00:26:26.224 --> 00:26:27.057
Yeah.

00:26:27.057 --> 00:26:28.350
It felt...

00:26:28.350 --> 00:26:29.183
Imperialist.

00:26:29.183 --> 00:26:30.330
It felt a little...

00:26:30.330 --> 00:26:32.100
I just felt a little uncomfortable.

00:26:32.100 --> 00:26:34.807
I mean, especially thinking of
the "White Lotus" of it all,

00:26:34.807 --> 00:26:37.740
and like, it was the
daughter who was like woke

00:26:37.740 --> 00:26:39.297
and like laying into 'em,

00:26:39.297 --> 00:26:42.150
and the daughter's friend who was like,

00:26:42.150 --> 00:26:43.830
seeing the other side of it.

00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:47.212
I didn't know exactly
how to feel about it.

00:26:47.212 --> 00:26:48.990
But it did make you think,

00:26:48.990 --> 00:26:50.370
it made you think twice about it,

00:26:50.370 --> 00:26:52.563
so you didn't just blindly enjoy it.

00:26:52.563 --> 00:26:55.741
The luau was, it was pretty
educational about like,

00:26:55.741 --> 00:27:00.741
the way that their, the Pacific Islanders,

00:27:01.202 --> 00:27:03.720
Hawaiian settlers, they would fish,

00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:07.920
and all the ingenuity of
the things they would do.

00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:09.960
But yeah, it's like...

00:27:09.960 --> 00:27:11.450
Yeah, it just felt...

00:27:12.540 --> 00:27:14.520
Yeah, I don't know what to say.

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:15.900
It felt very American.

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:17.550
Yeah.

00:27:17.550 --> 00:27:18.423
Yeah.

00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:20.153
Yeah.

00:27:21.169 --> 00:27:22.002
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:27:22.002 --> 00:27:23.160
You felt like a colonizer.

00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:25.920
It's a good show though, because it puts,

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:26.753
it just...

00:27:27.990 --> 00:27:29.310
It puts it out there.

00:27:29.310 --> 00:27:31.740
Yeah, I mean, it's an
excellent show for that.

00:27:31.740 --> 00:27:33.180
And the music is great too.

00:27:33.180 --> 00:27:34.770
It made you have a more difficult time

00:27:34.770 --> 00:27:36.180
enjoying your Hawaii vacation.

00:27:36.180 --> 00:27:37.200
Right, mission accomplished.

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:38.820
Yeah, right, yeah.

00:27:38.820 --> 00:27:39.653
Yeah.

00:27:39.653 --> 00:27:40.740
That's all I'll say about that,

00:27:40.740 --> 00:27:42.903
but the scuba diving of it all, you know,

00:27:43.950 --> 00:27:47.250
we planned a trip in like
day three or day four,

00:27:47.250 --> 00:27:49.710
and then we skipped a number of days,

00:27:49.710 --> 00:27:51.570
and then went to a different place.

00:27:51.570 --> 00:27:55.800
So the first day we went out on a boat

00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:57.120
with a group of people

00:27:57.120 --> 00:28:00.723
who were all scuba diving
to Molokini Crater.

00:28:03.120 --> 00:28:07.650
You can see this like strip
of land out in between

00:28:07.650 --> 00:28:12.063
our beach and the next island over, Lanai.

00:28:13.050 --> 00:28:14.837
So it's half of this crater that-

00:28:14.837 --> 00:28:16.680
That's the one that like the Microsoft guy

00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:17.973
owns most of it, right?

00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:20.130
The Oracle guy.

00:28:20.130 --> 00:28:20.963
Oracle guy.

00:28:20.963 --> 00:28:23.697
Yep, he owns, basically owns all of it.

00:28:23.697 --> 00:28:28.697
That island used to be
a do pineapple farm,

00:28:29.310 --> 00:28:31.050
like the whole thing,

00:28:31.050 --> 00:28:33.900
and then he bought the whole thing.

00:28:33.900 --> 00:28:37.740
And then there's one resort on there,

00:28:37.740 --> 00:28:40.680
and then there's people who
live at the top of the island,

00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:43.713
and then they all work
at the resort, basically.

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:46.470
We were actually gonna stay there,

00:28:46.470 --> 00:28:48.450
but Christie didn't want to
take a second plane ride,

00:28:48.450 --> 00:28:50.310
because she hates flying on plane so much.

00:28:50.310 --> 00:28:51.210
And I was like, you know what?

00:28:51.210 --> 00:28:52.170
That's fine.

00:28:52.170 --> 00:28:54.810
I don't think there's anything
to do over there, anyway.

00:28:54.810 --> 00:28:57.090
You can like rent a Jeep and
like drive the Jeep around

00:28:57.090 --> 00:28:59.550
all over the island,
which would've been fun.

00:28:59.550 --> 00:29:00.789
But, yeah.

00:29:00.789 --> 00:29:03.390
We actually went close on
our second scuba diving,

00:29:03.390 --> 00:29:06.560
but the first one was
Molokini Crater, and...

00:29:08.820 --> 00:29:10.770
It was the first time for everything,

00:29:10.770 --> 00:29:12.720
except technically diving.

00:29:12.720 --> 00:29:15.240
Like diving off of a
boat, diving with a group,

00:29:15.240 --> 00:29:17.493
like having an orientation.

00:29:19.758 --> 00:29:22.020
Them getting your tanks
ready, and everything.

00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:24.120
Everything was new, but
they made it really easy,

00:29:24.120 --> 00:29:25.020
and you kind of...

00:29:26.340 --> 00:29:28.140
A guy jumps in the water with you,

00:29:28.140 --> 00:29:31.260
and there was a group of like six of us,

00:29:31.260 --> 00:29:34.440
and then Lincoln and I
were of course buddies.

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:38.160
So even though you have a
guide, it's really up to, like,

00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:40.890
you have to be responsible
for your own safety.

00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:43.800
You can't depend on anybody else,

00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:47.167
some guide to make sure that you're safe,

00:29:47.167 --> 00:29:48.780
and to check everything for you,

00:29:48.780 --> 00:29:50.400
you gotta be responsible for yourself.

00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:52.980
That's why there's so much
training and certification,

00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:57.120
but then you learn to rely
on a buddy to stay together,

00:29:57.120 --> 00:29:59.995
and to like, keep an eye on
each other and communicate,

00:29:59.995 --> 00:30:02.160
and help each other.

00:30:02.160 --> 00:30:05.700
Like, worst case, if
you needed to get air,

00:30:05.700 --> 00:30:07.560
like if you run outta air
or something goes wrong,

00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:09.150
like they can give you their spare air,

00:30:09.150 --> 00:30:10.560
and that type of stuff,

00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:12.630
and help you get back to the surface.

00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:14.040
So like, Lincoln and I buddied up,

00:30:14.040 --> 00:30:15.930
but we were in a group that was like,

00:30:15.930 --> 00:30:19.770
you get in the water, and
then you descend to like 30,

00:30:19.770 --> 00:30:21.180
40, 50 feet.

00:30:21.180 --> 00:30:23.742
And then on this first dive,

00:30:23.742 --> 00:30:27.540
he's taking us around on
the outside of the crater,

00:30:27.540 --> 00:30:29.400
and it's, I mean,

00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:34.400
it's like flying beside
a mountain, you know?

00:30:35.550 --> 00:30:39.810
You're just suspended
in water, in this, like,

00:30:39.810 --> 00:30:41.430
and it's just a sheer,

00:30:41.430 --> 00:30:46.430
I would say it's like a 60
degree slope that just, whew,

00:30:48.360 --> 00:30:51.840
just goes down, and it seems
like it just goes down forever.

00:30:51.840 --> 00:30:53.580
Like, if you didn't watch yourself,

00:30:53.580 --> 00:30:58.580
you could just swim down
to like a crazy depth.

00:30:59.241 --> 00:31:01.860
What's some maximum
depth that you went to?

00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:03.033
That we went to?

00:31:04.350 --> 00:31:05.553
55 feet.

00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:07.530
That's pretty deep.

00:31:07.530 --> 00:31:10.050
Yeah, and so like on your left side,

00:31:10.050 --> 00:31:13.860
as we're like curving around,
it's just this whole wall

00:31:13.860 --> 00:31:17.550
of just underwater mountain side.

00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:20.010
And there's like some creatures
that he would point out,

00:31:20.010 --> 00:31:21.480
and stuff like that.

00:31:21.480 --> 00:31:26.310
But then on the right, it
just goes into like deep blue.

00:31:26.310 --> 00:31:27.143
It's just, whew,

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:30.030
like straight out, straight down.

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:32.610
It's just like, you just get this sense

00:31:32.610 --> 00:31:35.580
of just being so small.

00:31:35.580 --> 00:31:38.280
And like a shark's gonna
come out of the blue depths?

00:31:38.280 --> 00:31:41.610
And a shark swam out of the blue depths,

00:31:41.610 --> 00:31:44.790
and like, I would say it
was 40 feet away, but yeah,

00:31:44.790 --> 00:31:45.623
it was like a-

00:31:45.623 --> 00:31:46.456
How big, what kind?

00:31:46.456 --> 00:31:49.980
A white tipped shark.

00:31:49.980 --> 00:31:51.270
There may be another word in there.

00:31:51.270 --> 00:31:53.940
I can't remember, but
like a white tipped shark,

00:31:53.940 --> 00:31:55.690
I would say it was probably

00:31:56.880 --> 00:32:00.990
six feet long, was just
swimming out there.

00:32:00.990 --> 00:32:04.800
And, at a separate point
I looked out there,

00:32:04.800 --> 00:32:06.510
and there was a big ray,

00:32:06.510 --> 00:32:10.743
not a manta ray, but an an eagle
ray is what they're called.

00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:14.043
So it's like, hey, this is what I was...

00:32:14.043 --> 00:32:17.010
This is kind of what
you hope for, you know?

00:32:17.010 --> 00:32:18.000
You're swimming out there

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:21.060
and seeing this freaking
wildlife, you're seeing a shark,

00:32:21.060 --> 00:32:23.180
you're seeing an eagle ray, just like...

00:32:24.090 --> 00:32:26.250
How big was that?
Just doing it's thing.

00:32:26.250 --> 00:32:29.430
Probably five feet wing
span on this thing.

00:32:29.430 --> 00:32:31.740
I mean, it was, again,

00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:34.830
it might have been 40 feet away,

00:32:34.830 --> 00:32:37.440
'cause we were staying close to the edge.

00:32:37.440 --> 00:32:41.430
And then if you, he said
at the end of this thing,

00:32:41.430 --> 00:32:43.530
there's a shark cleaning station.

00:32:43.530 --> 00:32:45.150
Shark cleaning station?

00:32:45.150 --> 00:32:47.550
It's not where a bunch of
scuba divers go around a shark

00:32:47.550 --> 00:32:49.410
and just start scrubbing it with brushes.

00:32:49.410 --> 00:32:51.420
But it's where like little fish would,

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:52.980
a shark would go there and-

00:32:52.980 --> 00:32:54.330
Get the little, yeah.

00:32:54.330 --> 00:32:56.310
He knows that these
little fishes are gonna

00:32:56.310 --> 00:32:57.420
eat this stuff I'm covered in.

00:32:57.420 --> 00:32:59.790
It's like making my own clean.

00:32:59.790 --> 00:33:02.040
Did you see this in action?

00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:07.040
We ran out of air before we got to that.

00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:08.610
Everybody, or just you and Lincoln?

00:33:08.610 --> 00:33:09.720
Just me and Lincoln.

00:33:09.720 --> 00:33:10.553
This is our first dive.

00:33:10.553 --> 00:33:11.640
You've been breathing too hard.

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:12.930
You're breathing too hard.

00:33:12.930 --> 00:33:15.870
Well, actually, I looked around
and I couldn't find Lincoln.

00:33:15.870 --> 00:33:17.460
I'm like, oh crap.

00:33:17.460 --> 00:33:18.293
You lost your buddy?

00:33:18.293 --> 00:33:19.126
Where is Lincoln?

00:33:19.126 --> 00:33:21.480
And they train you, like
if you lose your buddy...

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:22.650
Panic.

00:33:22.650 --> 00:33:23.880
Yeah, just panic.

00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:24.713
Just panic.

00:33:24.713 --> 00:33:26.026
Just start sucking in water.

00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:27.960
Crap your pants.

00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:29.040
It's over for both of you.

00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:32.370
Ink, and just do the
human version of an ink,

00:33:32.370 --> 00:33:34.470
which is like sharting.

00:33:34.470 --> 00:33:36.420
No, it's like, you're supposed,

00:33:36.420 --> 00:33:37.860
if you can't see him, you look up,

00:33:37.860 --> 00:33:40.230
you look down, and then
you start to ascend,

00:33:40.230 --> 00:33:41.940
and you look around again and again.

00:33:41.940 --> 00:33:45.870
But I just looked up, and I
could see him up there 30 feet,

00:33:45.870 --> 00:33:49.620
and he was already going
up, 'cause he was like,

00:33:49.620 --> 00:33:52.830
very low on air, and he
kind of got a little scared,

00:33:52.830 --> 00:33:54.750
and instead of swimming
over and tapping me

00:33:54.750 --> 00:33:58.320
on the shoulder and
telling me, let's go up.

00:33:58.320 --> 00:33:59.940
Here's the signal.
Violated the buddy system.

00:33:59.940 --> 00:34:01.860
He got a little ahead of
himself and he was like,

00:34:01.860 --> 00:34:03.750
oh crap, I gotta get outta here.

00:34:03.750 --> 00:34:07.080
But you still have to
ascend at a slow rate.

00:34:07.080 --> 00:34:09.985
So how long, approximately?

00:34:09.985 --> 00:34:11.838
50 or 55 feet.

00:34:11.838 --> 00:34:14.940
I think our dive was like 36 minutes,

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:16.233
and there were probably people who were

00:34:16.233 --> 00:34:18.090
down there for 45 minutes.

00:34:18.090 --> 00:34:20.280
No, but once you realized
that you're low on air,

00:34:20.280 --> 00:34:23.760
like, what's the minimum
amount of time that you need

00:34:23.760 --> 00:34:27.273
in order to ascend 60
feet back to the surface?

00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:29.980
I should know that, shouldn't I?

00:34:29.980 --> 00:34:32.070
Isn't that part of like
the math and stuff?

00:34:32.070 --> 00:34:33.243
Oh, I don't do math.

00:34:34.275 --> 00:34:37.440
But, well you don't let it get below 500,

00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:39.150
and then there's no issue.

00:34:39.150 --> 00:34:42.090
Like, when you're down
there at 50 or 60 feet,

00:34:42.090 --> 00:34:44.730
it's like, yeah, you're
not gonna have any problem.

00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:46.410
It's like, once you get to that, but like,

00:34:46.410 --> 00:34:47.648
if you forget about it,

00:34:47.648 --> 00:34:50.430
then I actually don't
know the answer to that.

00:34:50.430 --> 00:34:51.530
Don't let that happen.

00:34:53.130 --> 00:34:55.110
Well, you might need to pay attention,

00:34:55.110 --> 00:34:56.509
or read the book..
Listen man,

00:34:56.509 --> 00:34:58.023
I bet Lincoln knows.

00:34:58.920 --> 00:35:01.320
But Lincoln, well he is
doing well with this.

00:35:01.320 --> 00:35:03.000
Like, he's not...

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.560
He's enjoying it.

00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:05.393
He's not scared.

00:35:05.393 --> 00:35:08.430
A lot of it was me
watching him swim around,

00:35:08.430 --> 00:35:11.370
and just getting enjoyment outta the fact

00:35:11.370 --> 00:35:12.870
that he was enjoying it.

00:35:12.870 --> 00:35:14.746
The fact that I had an
idea to do something,

00:35:14.746 --> 00:35:19.230
and I got him to put in the
work, and then he's loving it.

00:35:19.230 --> 00:35:21.420
It was one of the highlights of the trip.

00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:23.160
From basically just like "White Lotus",

00:35:23.160 --> 00:35:25.323
except you succeeded.

00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:28.800
You succeeded in what that dad...

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:31.530
That dad was like trying to
get his son to do something,

00:35:31.530 --> 00:35:33.067
to connect with him,

00:35:33.067 --> 00:35:37.620
but not really succeeding, but
you actually pulled it off.

00:35:37.620 --> 00:35:39.131
It worked on our account.

00:35:39.131 --> 00:35:39.964
Yeah.

00:35:39.964 --> 00:35:40.797
Yeah.

00:35:40.797 --> 00:35:41.943
The second trip we did,

00:35:43.080 --> 00:35:44.370
we went with a different outfit.

00:35:44.370 --> 00:35:47.460
We had to drive further, and
then get on a different boat

00:35:47.460 --> 00:35:50.730
that went to Lanai.

00:35:50.730 --> 00:35:54.300
So we're like, we get
to go around that island

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:56.580
and see the one resort on the island,

00:35:56.580 --> 00:36:00.600
and then how barren it
is, and how wild it is.

00:36:00.600 --> 00:36:01.433
And then-

00:36:01.433 --> 00:36:02.700
Is it like, trees?

00:36:02.700 --> 00:36:03.720
Is it all trees?

00:36:03.720 --> 00:36:05.430
There's not a lot of trees, no,

00:36:05.430 --> 00:36:08.910
because they clear cut everything for

00:36:08.910 --> 00:36:10.590
pineapples.
Pineapples.

00:36:10.590 --> 00:36:13.230
So now it's just, it's more deserty,

00:36:13.230 --> 00:36:16.560
like the type of brush
and everything on it,

00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:18.930
and our side of Maui was that way too.

00:36:18.930 --> 00:36:20.490
When you go to the other side,

00:36:20.490 --> 00:36:22.440
there's like a tremendous
amount of rainfall,

00:36:22.440 --> 00:36:24.390
and it's a totally different ecosystem.

00:36:24.390 --> 00:36:27.600
Probably a lot more like
the Kauai experience.

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:29.190
I just didn't take the road to Hana,

00:36:29.190 --> 00:36:30.150
so I can't speak to it.
That's basically

00:36:30.150 --> 00:36:32.850
what I've heard is that Maui has...

00:36:32.850 --> 00:36:35.940
It's the best combination of everything

00:36:35.940 --> 00:36:38.730
that you could get on
the other islands, so.

00:36:38.730 --> 00:36:40.397
But you didn't go to
that side, so you didn't

00:36:40.397 --> 00:36:41.230
get to see it.
Yeah,

00:36:41.230 --> 00:36:42.720
I didn't go to that side.

00:36:42.720 --> 00:36:45.870
I think that is my one regret.

00:36:45.870 --> 00:36:49.470
But that second dive trip was
even better than the first one

00:36:49.470 --> 00:36:50.400
to Molokini Crater,

00:36:50.400 --> 00:36:53.130
because we went to what
are called The Cathedrals.

00:36:53.130 --> 00:36:56.645
You've got these volcanic rock formations

00:36:56.645 --> 00:37:00.810
where there's all these crevasses,

00:37:00.810 --> 00:37:04.080
crevasse, and tunnels.

00:37:04.080 --> 00:37:05.280
We jump out of the boat.

00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:06.301
Can't go on those.

00:37:06.301 --> 00:37:08.220
We get our group together,

00:37:08.220 --> 00:37:12.630
and the first thing we did was
swim down to about 35 feet,

00:37:12.630 --> 00:37:13.980
maybe 30 feet,

00:37:13.980 --> 00:37:17.070
and then I saw that some
people in our group,

00:37:17.070 --> 00:37:18.600
all of a sudden, they turn on flashlights.

00:37:18.600 --> 00:37:21.183
I'm like, well damn, I
don't have a flashlight.

00:37:22.020 --> 00:37:23.850
This wasn't discussed?

00:37:23.850 --> 00:37:25.650
They mentioned some about
a flashlight on the boat.

00:37:25.650 --> 00:37:28.830
Like if you have a flashlight,
blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:37:28.830 --> 00:37:30.480
And once they said, if
you have a flashlight,

00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:31.803
I don't have one.

00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:33.713
Okay.

00:37:33.713 --> 00:37:36.690
So we start going through
a bonafide tunnel,

00:37:36.690 --> 00:37:41.690
a tunnel that ended up being
probably, from wall to wall,

00:37:44.610 --> 00:37:47.460
not much more than 10 feet.

00:37:47.460 --> 00:37:48.293
How long is this tunnel?

00:37:48.293 --> 00:37:50.883
10 feet in diameter, and then I would say,

00:37:52.585 --> 00:37:57.030
it might have been 25 feet in length.

00:37:57.030 --> 00:37:59.130
It opened up to more of big ocean.

00:37:59.130 --> 00:38:00.270
Yeah.

00:38:00.270 --> 00:38:01.103
Yeah.

00:38:01.103 --> 00:38:02.596
Not one of these endless
caves that you die in.

00:38:02.596 --> 00:38:04.290
No, it wasn't going down.

00:38:04.290 --> 00:38:06.933
It was totally horizontal, and like,

00:38:07.770 --> 00:38:10.020
it was the first thing we
went through, and I was like,

00:38:10.020 --> 00:38:12.462
oh my gosh, this is crazy.

00:38:12.462 --> 00:38:15.210
The main thing you're learning
to do when you're learning

00:38:15.210 --> 00:38:19.200
to scuba dive is like, is
to regulate your buoyancy,

00:38:19.200 --> 00:38:23.910
regulate your depth in the
water using your flotation,

00:38:23.910 --> 00:38:28.384
like adding air or removing
air from it so that you're not,

00:38:28.384 --> 00:38:30.810
in this case, scraping against the top

00:38:30.810 --> 00:38:32.733
or the bottom of the tunnel.

00:38:34.200 --> 00:38:35.970
It was so much fun.

00:38:35.970 --> 00:38:37.740
And then after that, we're going down

00:38:37.740 --> 00:38:42.210
into these like other little,
little archway tunnels,

00:38:42.210 --> 00:38:45.813
like swimming through all of
those type of rock formations.

00:38:46.860 --> 00:38:51.270
Oh, it was such a payoff to the work

00:38:51.270 --> 00:38:53.580
that we put in to get certified.

00:38:53.580 --> 00:38:56.460
I can't wait to go
scuba diving again, man.

00:38:56.460 --> 00:39:00.720
I'm trying to plan a trip
now for me and Lincoln,

00:39:00.720 --> 00:39:02.220
I asked Chase if he wanted to go,

00:39:02.220 --> 00:39:04.320
and he's the only other
person at Mythical I know of

00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:08.130
who's scuba certified to go
out to the Channel Islands.

00:39:08.130 --> 00:39:08.970
Yeah.

00:39:08.970 --> 00:39:12.510
And do that, but there were
dudes with beards, man.

00:39:12.510 --> 00:39:14.340
You're saying you don't wanna do it

00:39:14.340 --> 00:39:16.680
because you got this mustache.

00:39:16.680 --> 00:39:17.760
No, no, I've been-

00:39:17.760 --> 00:39:18.780
You gotta figure it out.

00:39:18.780 --> 00:39:20.669
I've heard many people say that you could

00:39:20.669 --> 00:39:21.502
figure it out.
You would absolutely

00:39:21.502 --> 00:39:22.335
love it.

00:39:22.335 --> 00:39:23.790
But I...

00:39:23.790 --> 00:39:25.560
In the little bit of
snorkeling that I've done,

00:39:25.560 --> 00:39:28.410
when I like used the stuff
that they said to use,

00:39:28.410 --> 00:39:30.481
like the silicone-like stuff,

00:39:30.481 --> 00:39:33.330
it was just like I have to get somebody

00:39:33.330 --> 00:39:37.890
who actually knows what to
do, to tell me what to do

00:39:37.890 --> 00:39:40.860
versus just going on the internet and...

00:39:40.860 --> 00:39:42.510
You know.

00:39:42.510 --> 00:39:44.640
It's totally, I mean,
you gotta figure it out.

00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:47.310
Like, Shepherd's a strong swimmer, right?

00:39:47.310 --> 00:39:48.143
Yeah.

00:39:48.143 --> 00:39:48.976
He would love it.

00:39:48.976 --> 00:39:50.610
Yeah, he'd be into it.

00:39:50.610 --> 00:39:52.890
You know I'm not a strong
swimmer, it's not about that,

00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:55.530
but like you're so
comfortable in the water.

00:39:55.530 --> 00:39:57.810
Yeah, I mean, I'm
definitely intrigued by it.

00:39:57.810 --> 00:40:02.810
I mean, I was thinking
about going spear fishing

00:40:03.060 --> 00:40:04.710
with a friend that does that,

00:40:04.710 --> 00:40:05.850
because that's more just like,

00:40:05.850 --> 00:40:07.770
put on the snorkel and hold
your breath for a long time,

00:40:07.770 --> 00:40:08.790
which I can do.

00:40:08.790 --> 00:40:10.306
Yeah, you can do that.

00:40:10.306 --> 00:40:12.297
No, I'm definitely interested in it.

00:40:12.297 --> 00:40:14.640
And I think Shepherd, I know
shepherd would be into it.

00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:17.070
He would be like, "Sure, I'll do it."

00:40:17.070 --> 00:40:19.650
Yeah, it's...

00:40:19.650 --> 00:40:22.590
I mean, and I wasn't, I still
am not comfortable enough

00:40:22.590 --> 00:40:24.720
to like completely enjoy myself, because,

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:26.520
again, everything and taking out a boat

00:40:26.520 --> 00:40:27.570
and going with a guide,

00:40:27.570 --> 00:40:30.780
and like people giving you
orientation and all that,

00:40:30.780 --> 00:40:32.220
everything's still so new.

00:40:32.220 --> 00:40:34.350
And then you get in the
water, and you're like,

00:40:34.350 --> 00:40:36.870
you're learning how to
use the dive computer,

00:40:36.870 --> 00:40:41.040
and how to follow people,
but not too close.

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:44.340
Everything's kind of,
you're figuring it out,

00:40:44.340 --> 00:40:45.173
and I...

00:40:46.635 --> 00:40:48.000
Yeah, so there was a lot on my mind,

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:50.790
but my instructor told me, he was like,

00:40:50.790 --> 00:40:53.850
after you get a certain amount
of dives under your belt,

00:40:53.850 --> 00:40:57.510
then it becomes this total zen experience.

00:40:57.510 --> 00:40:58.493
You stop thinking about

00:40:58.493 --> 00:40:59.820
all of it.
Where you can be...

00:40:59.820 --> 00:41:02.490
Being in the water is
totally being in the moment,

00:41:02.490 --> 00:41:05.370
and he said, and when you
come back out on land,

00:41:05.370 --> 00:41:07.050
you look at the world differently.

00:41:07.050 --> 00:41:10.084
You start to look vertically,

00:41:10.084 --> 00:41:15.084
like we tend to work in like
a horizontal plane, you know?

00:41:15.671 --> 00:41:18.270
'Cause we're not birds,

00:41:18.270 --> 00:41:20.550
but he said you start to
bring more of that back

00:41:20.550 --> 00:41:22.173
into your experience on land.

00:41:22.173 --> 00:41:23.850
Have you been looking up more?

00:41:23.850 --> 00:41:25.860
You start looking up more.

00:41:25.860 --> 00:41:27.690
Took a walk from my house,

00:41:27.690 --> 00:41:29.760
and I was like, oh, look
at the trees up there.

00:41:29.760 --> 00:41:31.380
Wonder if I could fly up there to them.

00:41:31.380 --> 00:41:32.213
Just..

00:41:33.177 --> 00:41:34.385
Just kind of float up.

00:41:34.385 --> 00:41:35.580
It's...

00:41:35.580 --> 00:41:36.630
Don't get any ideas.

00:41:36.630 --> 00:41:38.130
It's great, man.

00:41:38.130 --> 00:41:40.410
That's the whole nother
thing is to get those

00:41:42.630 --> 00:41:43.833
backpack fans.

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:46.907
Maybe I get into that.

00:41:46.907 --> 00:41:47.740
What do you mean a back?

00:41:47.740 --> 00:41:49.500
Oh, you're talking about like a jet pack?

00:41:49.500 --> 00:41:50.730
Powered parachute.

00:41:50.730 --> 00:41:51.563
Oh.

00:41:51.563 --> 00:41:52.519
And Jesse won't let me know.

00:41:52.519 --> 00:41:54.210
She's afraid I'm gonna die.

00:41:54.210 --> 00:41:55.533
This is better than that.

00:41:57.090 --> 00:41:58.700
There's a lot more freedom,
and there's not like

00:41:58.700 --> 00:42:00.600
propelling.
It's safer.

00:42:00.600 --> 00:42:01.433
It's gotta be safe.

00:42:01.433 --> 00:42:02.460
It's definitely safer.

00:42:02.460 --> 00:42:04.342
We also did an ATV trip,

00:42:04.342 --> 00:42:09.342
which was not nearly as good
as the ATV trip that like,

00:42:10.290 --> 00:42:14.193
when we were in Kauai and
we went with the boys,

00:42:15.150 --> 00:42:17.040
and we were like in those quads

00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:19.680
and we went through
this like bamboo forest,

00:42:19.680 --> 00:42:21.180
and we went to this place that had a

00:42:21.180 --> 00:42:22.740
waterfall.
It was good.

00:42:22.740 --> 00:42:27.740
Well, this was on an old pineapple farm.

00:42:28.500 --> 00:42:30.060
There's so many of 'em in Maui,

00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:33.840
and they were given permission to turn it,

00:42:33.840 --> 00:42:35.907
since they're not growing
pineapples anymore...

00:42:35.907 --> 00:42:37.867
Who grows the pineapples now?

00:42:37.867 --> 00:42:40.500
They're not growing any
they are or in Lanai,

00:42:40.500 --> 00:42:41.333
I don't know.

00:42:42.990 --> 00:42:45.243
I think they're all grown in a lab, man.

00:42:48.265 --> 00:42:49.800
So you got this ATV course,

00:42:49.800 --> 00:42:54.300
and there's like all of this
black plastic coming up.

00:42:54.300 --> 00:42:57.153
And so they stop and
explain at a certain point,

00:42:58.320 --> 00:43:02.313
there are layers upon
layers of black plastic.

00:43:03.180 --> 00:43:06.330
You see like gardens where
people would plant stuff

00:43:06.330 --> 00:43:08.220
and like to keep the weed.
It's part of the farming.

00:43:08.220 --> 00:43:09.180
Keep the weeds out,

00:43:09.180 --> 00:43:11.460
they'll like poke a hole,
and plant something,

00:43:11.460 --> 00:43:13.980
and then they'll water
underneath the plastic

00:43:13.980 --> 00:43:16.347
so it conserves water.

00:43:16.347 --> 00:43:20.580
And it was a farming technique
that actually destroyed

00:43:20.580 --> 00:43:23.170
the land there, where
what they would do is

00:43:24.060 --> 00:43:27.810
after a season of pineapples,

00:43:27.810 --> 00:43:30.270
then they would like till it up,

00:43:30.270 --> 00:43:32.700
and then put another layer of plastic,

00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:34.230
and just do that again and again

00:43:34.230 --> 00:43:35.280
to the point where it's like,

00:43:35.280 --> 00:43:38.847
you go 8, 10, 12, 16 feet down,

00:43:38.847 --> 00:43:41.550
and it's just layers of plastic

00:43:41.550 --> 00:43:43.530
where they would just decimate the land.

00:43:43.530 --> 00:43:45.390
People do so much stupid stuff.

00:43:45.390 --> 00:43:47.730
I know, it was so depressing.

00:43:47.730 --> 00:43:50.370
But the cool thing about the ATV place

00:43:50.370 --> 00:43:53.100
we went was that like, they're
rehabilitating the land.

00:43:53.100 --> 00:43:55.860
There's no way you can
pull out all that plastic,

00:43:55.860 --> 00:44:00.540
but what you can do is
that you can replant trees

00:44:00.540 --> 00:44:02.250
on top of it.

00:44:02.250 --> 00:44:04.440
And like, there was a whole part that they

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:08.106
had never planted
pineapples up on the hill,

00:44:08.106 --> 00:44:10.197
and so there were still a forest up there.

00:44:10.197 --> 00:44:11.550
And they said, look up there,

00:44:11.550 --> 00:44:15.240
you see all the rain
clouds above the forest?

00:44:15.240 --> 00:44:17.310
He was like the reason why
they planted pineapples here

00:44:17.310 --> 00:44:20.490
is because all of that rain was down here.

00:44:20.490 --> 00:44:23.080
And what I didn't realize was that once

